{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>That it may go well with me.</b> So that when you say <b>you are my sister</b>, each one of them will hope that I will give you to him in marriage, and none of them will plot to kill me, but will treat me well with a bride-price and gifts — as was the custom then, that they would entice the woman's father with a bride-price and her relatives with presents, in order that they agree to give her to the suitor. Therefore the Torah says: מָהֹר יִמְהָרֶנָּה... אִם מָאֵן יְמָאֵן אָבִיהָ כֶּסֶף יִשְׁקֹל (Exodus 22:15–16). And in the meantime, he intended to depart from there."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:54.885881862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}